 # Visual Hull Oracle Kernel
 
-Also called: Visual Hull Oracle, Oracle Kernel
 
 ## Overview
-The Visual Hull Oracle Kernel is a parallel processing unit that performs binary culling of voxels to determine if they intersect the visual hull surface $S(p) = 0.5$ [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently identifying which voxels in a sparse voxel grid contribute to the final volume by leveraging hierarchical mip pyramids over silhouette images to compute conservative bounds on voxel coverage [S1]. It is distinguished from sibling methods by its specific use of component-wise multiplication of conservative bounds across multiple camera views to make a definitive KEEP or CULL decision, building on the silhouette acquisition and filtering techniques described in [Silhouette Image Acquisition and Filtering](3754-silhouette-image-acquisition-and-filtering.md).
